  "context": "# Goal\nTameshi round 37, verification-fixture craft. Claims are frozen at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-37/contract.json. C1 calibration resolves the r36 empty-panel control's unreachable scratch input; C2 adds bounded Bash ANSI-C `$'...'` quote handling to tools/tally-audit-v3.py and re-attests the frozen r36 counter. Source S104 is opened this round at the official GNU Bash 5.3 source.\n\n# Planner and roles\nThe L1 holds the canonical planner seat; a bounded planning data-walk rides the scout/connector items. Wave 1 contains the required connector, 3+ executors, scribe, scout, reviewer, and critic roles. Do not invent a planner role or pass a model; taxonomy roles route through /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/config.yml.\n\n# Hard write and process bounds\nLane repo: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin. Every `Report:` trailer is relative to that lane root: write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/<that path>. Each writer must use its own actual worktree, unique branch/path, and observed base; no concurrent writers on the live checkout. Seats are leaves, never spawn. Never mutate the lane Git index, jj state, `.git`, `.ufo/state`, fleet repo, sibling lane, or source tree. Write only the assigned report under `.ufo/waves/round-37/w1/`; findings are read-only.\n\n# Tooling\nOperator tooling authorization: install/update tools that help via official sources, with channel order pacman only after its safety gate, then uv tool, official release binary, cargo/npm; record any install/version/channel/reason. Pacman transactions are PAUSED host-wide: do not run pacman; use uv/npx/official binary if needed. No tool is required for this item unless its evidence proves otherwise.\n\n# Claims and falsification\nDo not widen the frozen predicates. C1's before is one r36 evidence/input mismatch; the target is zero only when the committed empty-panel specification and both v1/v2 receipts resolve. C2's frozen two-case predicate requires blanking the trailing shell comment after an escaped ANSI-C quote while preserving a literal `#` inside the quoted string. The tool is not a full Bash lexer; nested substitutions and unquoted line continuations remain explicit holds. Report adverse or inconclusive evidence, do not repair it in another item.",
